nch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064177: Remove recently-added viewBox attrs from outer SVG element in SVG assets, so we can benefit from the automatically synthesized one (and get preserveAspectRatio=\"none\" for free).  a=RyanVM\n\nThis viewBox attribute was unnecessary and slightly counterproductive, so\nit's nicer to just remove it.\n\nThe explicit viewBox was unnecessary because Gecko will automatically\nsynthesize an appropriate viewBox (if the attribute is missing) on the\noutermost SVG element in an SVG image, using the SVG element's declared 'width'\nand 'height' attributes.  So, it's nice for conciseness to benefit from this\nand avoid needing to manually repeat the width and height in two spots on the\nsame element.\n\nThe explicit viewBox was counter-productive because: if we omit it and instead\nallow Gecko to synthesize a viewBox, Gecko will also automatically apply\npreserveAspectRatio=\"none\" *by default*, which is essentially always the\nbehavior we really want our SVG assets to have. On the other hand, if a viewBox\nis explicitly provided on the outermost SVG element, then Gecko uses the SVG\nspec's default `preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid\"` behavior, which is essentially\na \"contain\" constraint and can cause subly unexpected positioning glitches like\nhttps://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2063751 in cases where slight\npixel-rounding issues can cause the aspect ratio to be ever-so-slightly off\nfrom the image's natural aspect ratio.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319252\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319537\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/downloads/notification-finish-animation.svg", "browser/themes/shared/downloads/notification-start-animation.svg", "browser/themes/shared/downloads/progress-ring-20.svg", "browser/themes/shared/icons/success-animation.svg"], "git_node": "d1d973c6bd5480affd330a098641c29c986d97cf", "git_parents": ["f394d973931a0738ba455ba46b9a7056ee42f711"], "node": "2ed8a5189cd6f79c1d1ae4448133f2c8159a0738", "parents": ["94853a37adb93d49fde2bbb6c47d08e6c6a01ef5"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787076339, "git_changesets": ["f394d973931a0738ba455ba46b9a7056ee42f711", "d1d973c6bd5480affd330a098641c29c986d97cf"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28059": {"changesets": [{"author": "Dana Keeler \u003cdkeeler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063132 - properly determine TLS handshake auth curve for ECDSA  a=RyanVM\n\nThis also takes the opportunity to avoid some unnecessary work when gathering\nkey exchange and auth curve telemetry.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318852\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319562\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/metrics.yaml", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSCallbacks.cpp"], "git_node": "69179619b28fdff4b5f52f6ce2d685359e0447c5", "git_parents": ["d1d973c6bd5480affd330a098641c29c986d97cf"], "node": "c2f1b2a0ccc27811c847e1c8613199a43b064a5d", "parents": ["2ed8a5189cd6f79c1d1ae4448133f2c8159a0738"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787076450, "git_changesets": ["69179619b28fdff4b5f52f6ce2d685359e0447c5"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28060": {"changesets": [{"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059274 - Allow LNA from insecure pages for now  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317783\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319551\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/test/browser/browser_test_lna_insecure_context.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "2bbece084ffc86051479e7be1cd97b40acc01ede", "git_parents": ["69179619b28fdff4b5f52f6ce2d685359e0447c5"], "node": "66068e69788f6301a5046be37afe90bc0ace7854", "parents": ["c2f1b2a0ccc27811c847e1c8613199a43b064a5d"], "tags": []}], "date":