a380f2038b87063b1ed293ac"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28112": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062119 - Do not dereference gJarHandler after it has been cleared at shutdown.  a=RyanVM\n\nnsJARChannel read the gJarHandler global directly in five places. Since bug\n1412726 that global is a StaticRefPtr cleared by ClearOnShutdown, so it can be\nnull while channels are still alive and opening a channel during late shutdown\ncrashes. The owning reference the channel takes in its constructor kept the\nhandler object alive but stopped protecting the global, and has had no readers\nsince that same bug.\n\nAdd shutdown safe accessors that return null once the singleton is gone, use\nthem for all of those accesses and fail the channel with\nNS_ERROR_ILLEGAL_DURING_SHUTDOWN instead. Drop the unused mJarHandler member.\n\nWhile here, EnsureCached can use the accessor instead of fetching the handler\nthrough the IO service and downcasting the result.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317420\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320107\n", "files": ["modules/libjar/nsJARChannel.cpp", "modules/libjar/nsJARChannel.h", "modules/libjar/nsJARProtocolHandler.cpp", "modules/libjar/nsJARProtocolHandler.h"], "git_node": "e25d603e00eb3474c9f0d93e0e241b067a414b0a", "git_parents": ["f6a523b77869d27da380f2038b87063b1ed293ac"], "node": "d787edde1a11522376a951bb61b39f5f9dc5d3a1", "parents": ["7e6f98246caa7a3054b0900a9c3dcb7c72f19907"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062119 - Clear the jar protocol handler after the JS module loader is gone.  a=RyanVM\n\nChrome JS module loading reads from omni.ja through jar channels, and\nmozJSModuleLoader::UnloadLoaders() runs after the XPCOMShutdownFinal phase,\nwhich is the default phase for ClearOnShutdown. The handler was therefore\ncleared while chrome JS modules could still be imported, leaving a window in\nwhich those imports and any other late jar access fail.\n\nClear it at CCPostLastCycleCollection instead, which runs after UnloadLoaders().\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317421\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320108\n", "files": ["modules/libjar/nsJAR.cpp", "modules/libjar/nsJARProtocolHandler.cpp"], "git_node": "adb881fe792ebe38d9a9ac8a5372c83a63f7cbc8", "git_parents": ["e25d603e00eb3474c9f0d93e0e241b067a414b0a"], "node": "4c519c7563eb4585e27a8c2a6ba77a17d0346806", "parents": ["d787edde1a11522376a951bb61b39f5f9dc5d3a1"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787230729, "git_changesets": ["e25d603e00eb3474c9f0d93e0e241b067a414b0a", "adb881fe792ebe38d9a9ac8a5372c83a63f7cbc8"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28113": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jan Grulich \u003cjgrulich@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054624 - WebRTC backport: Video capture: cap resolution and null-check header metadata  a=RyanVM\n\nReject video dimensions that could overflow frame size calculations.\nHandle missing SPA_META_Header which is optional.\n\nThis is a simple backport of an WebRTC upstream change.\n\nUpstream commit: 01455efea7797cff42c5228b14c85ab3cdb4bdac\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319163\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319994\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_capture/linux/video_capture_pipewire.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/01455efea7.no-op-cherry-pick-msg"], "git_node": "704a7f4484d8d18c233bf8eb007bb50a903ac08a", "git_parents": ["adb881fe792ebe38d9a9ac8a5372c83a63f7cbc8"], "node": "0db7890139826372e06434ae6e80f73684982079", "parents": ["4c519c7563eb4585e27a8c2a6ba77a17d0346806"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787230815, "git_changesets": ["704a7f4484d8d18c233bf8eb007bb50a903ac08a"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28114": {"changesets": [{"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061397 - Tear down WebSocketChannelChild on the main thread,  a=RyanVM\n\nUse the same approach HttpChannelChild::Release() uses: dispatch off-main-thread\nreleases through the main thread with DecrementWithLimit\u003c2\u003e, so the count==1\nSendDeleteSelf and count==0 delete only run on the main thread where the IPDL\nreference is also released.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319530\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320030\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketChannelChild.cpp"], "git_node": "3a72eb4efcdab70a42f305cfdefaa4aecffeeb50", "git_parents": ["704a7f4484d8d18c233bf8eb007bb50a903ac08a"], "node": "82685b0f935fe89fe01650d56563148616d2ceb6", "parents": ["0db7890139826372e06434ae6e80f73684982079"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787231352, "git_changesets": ["3a72eb4efcdab70a42f305cfdefaa4aecffeeb50"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28115": {"changesets": [{"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057817 - ensure browser id handling is consistent,  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318490\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319953\n", "files": ["docshell/base/BrowsingContext.cpp"], "git_node": "ab08eff01fbfc6f5806e918ae625b8b103096e00", "git_parents": ["3a72eb4efcdab70a42f305cfdefaa4aecffeeb50"], "node": "da27eaa238d646648b8d52921a22bbf631fd5a90", "parents": ["82685b0f935fe89fe01650d56563148616d2ceb6"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787231374, "git_changesets": ["ab08eff01fbfc6f5806e918ae625b8b103096e00"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28116": {"changesets": [{"author": "Eitan Isaacson \u003ceitan@monotonous.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058652 - Don't truncate actor ID.  a=RyanVM\n\nMatch the type of the local actorID with the uint64 mActorID.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315425\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319905\n", "files": ["accessible/ipc/DocAccessibleParent.cpp"], "git_node": "c906b71878f343e93741a6966efbd75ee3249ad5", "git_parents": ["ab08eff01fbfc6f5806e918ae625b8b103096e00"], "node": "0e892de88d93c7cb10224da5d3c190d1d0e32556", "parents": ["da27eaa238d646648b8d52921a22bbf631fd5a90"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787231396, "git_changesets": ["c906b71878f343e93741a6966efbd75ee3249ad5"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28117": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jan Grulich \u003cjgrulich@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055703 - WebRTC backport: Screen capture: reject negative videocrop position values  a=RyanVM\n\nValidate that SPA_META_VideoCrop position coordinates are\nnon-negative before using them as offsets into the frame buffer.\n\nThis is a simple backport of an WebRTC upstream change.\n\nUpstream commit: f93c4fefee56b60876629d03df1ad01e203cc8c3\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319398\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319996\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/linux/wayland/shared_screencast_stream.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/f93c4fefee.no-op-cherry-pick-msg"], "git_node": "552c9239427c6e5392191dff0e08161e7dacde73", "git_parents": ["c906b71878f343e93741a6966efbd75ee3249ad5"], "node": "e5259eb036ef7e67965752e4687817a374d1ae2c", "parents": ["0e892de88d93c7cb10224da5d3c190d1d0e32556"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787231780, "git_changesets": ["552c9239427c6e5392191dff0e08161e7dacde73"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28118": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jan Grulich \u003cjgrulich@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058627 - WebRTC backport: Screen capture: check n_datas before accessing buffer data planes  a=RyanVM\n\nReturn early from ProcessBuffer when spa_buffer-\u003en_datas is zero\nto avoid out-of-bounds access on metadata-only buffers that carry\nno data planes.\n\nThis is a simple backport of an WebRTC upstream change.\n\nUpstream commit: 3ce78cdbd865ad8837d1ffae21553791e8ec491d\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319390\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319995\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/linux/wayland/shared_screencast_stream.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/3ce78cdbd8.no-op-cherry-pick-msg"], "git_node": "25b0a83bbcc22dc486704e208a573fc61f1291a4", "git_parents": ["552c9239427c6e5392191dff0e08161e7dacde73"], "node": "71d8702feb8eb13e32dd85db9d4009ef2eec42b4", "parents": ["e5259eb036ef7e67965752e4687817a374d1ae2c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787231806, "git_changesets": ["25b0a83bbcc22dc486704e208a573fc61f1291a4"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28119": {"changesets": [{"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061430 - Fall back to non-localized if localized datetime error message formatting fails.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319175\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320114\n", "files": ["dom/html/input/DateTimeInputTypes.cpp", "intl/components/src/FormatBuffer.h"], "git_node": "762e6e3941a93a017b4f0241feccd75a224eeab5", "git_parents": ["25b0a83bbcc22dc486704e208a573fc61f1291a4"], "node": "bb158eeeee840ae9628b8ec9f15f84ee6e85c577", "parents": ["71d8702feb8eb13e32dd85db9d4009ef2eec42b4"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787232481, "git_changesets": ["762e6e3941a93a017b4f0241feccd75a224eeab5"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28120": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nicholas Poon \u003cnpoon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064507 - When all active normal tabs are selected for deletion, don't remove inactive tabs  a=RyanVM\n\nwillTabsRemainAfterDeletion does not include inactive tabs but the deletion branch that happens due to the function evaluating to false also deletes inactive tabs. Also, note that deleteMultipleTabs now calls removeTabs instead of removeNormalTabs when no active normal tabs remain. This results in tab group assignments being deleted instead of tab groups being closed and tab group assignments are kept, as seen in TabGroupMiddleware.kt. This can be dealt with in a follow up\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319837\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320140\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/HomeScreenViewModel.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/TabsCleanupFeature.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/controller/TabManagerController.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/TabsCleanupFeatureTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/controller/DefaultTabManagerControllerTest.kt"], "git_node": "9d9337d91fc534825b39e821c83cd9db89a5979b", "git_parents": ["762e6e3941a93a017b4f0241feccd75a224eeab5"], "node": "92f6a6b6106feab7fd1312009235e20620b82f0f", "parents": ["bb158eeeee840ae9628b8ec9f15f84ee6e85c577"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787276450, "git_changesets": ["9d9337d91fc534825b39e821c83cd9db89a5979b"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28121": {"changesets": [{"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065007 - Redefine X11's Success macro to X11Success to avoid conflicts.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319993\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320035\n", "files": ["gfx/gl/GLContextProviderGLX.cpp", "gfx/src/X11UndefineNone.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatformGtk.cpp", "widget/gtk/WidgetUtilsGtk.cpp"], "git_node": "f0b76eba072821d62e74ebdbd8da9243a2ce3b84", "git_parents": ["9d9337d91fc534825b39e821c83cd9db89a5979b"], "node": "704ae14c9c0948107a1c3a49147e70f4df88885b", "parents": ["92f6a6b6106feab7fd1312009235e20620b82f0f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787276474, "git_changesets": ["f0b76eba072821d62e74ebdbd8da9243a2ce3b84"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28122": {"changesets": [{"author": "mimi \u003cmjung@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059393 - Revert using uncached defaultBrowserCheck for set to default app menu messages  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319181\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320201\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/modules/OnboardingMessageProvider.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "4c313dbae190ab6acc4e0823320df456a8bb2bd3", "git_parents": ["f0b76eba072821d62e74ebdbd8da9243a2ce3b84"], "node": "6b9fb5faa573d7d45936e3f829ebbd84d9ee6a39", "parents": ["704ae14c9c0948107a1c3a49147e70f4df88885b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787276493, "git_changesets": ["4c313dbae190ab6acc4e0823320df456a8bb2bd3"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28123": {"changesets": [{"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061477 - Add a View Tab Groups row to the Organize Tabs panel  a=RyanVM\n\nAuto Tab Grouping / 'Organize Tabs'\n\nFigma: https://www.figma.com/design/75Z1LtkCEUJWCxoY2KyNHv/Smart-Window-Q2?node-id=10208-85576&m=dev\n\nv0 Brief: https://docs.google.com/document/d/15_lGUTaAM6HFimBwkfBVPPCg_0ROGIyInNeLSPPb0NE/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.k0db31goubh2\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316913\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320173\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-group-tabs/smartwindow-group-tabs.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AutoTabGrouping.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_group_tabs_button.js", "browser/locales-preview/autoTabGrouping.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/smartwindowGroupTabs.css"], "git_node": "fa5662d6e39f8962e20c365e982759b914c65b8a", "git_parents": ["4c313dbae190ab6acc4e0823320df456a8bb2bd3"], "node": "1e495ce334000913a29fe27dbbcabe166040b61c", "parents": ["6b9fb5faa573d7d45936e3f829ebbd84d9ee6a39"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787276613, "git_changesets": ["fa5662d6e39f8962e20c365e982759b914c65b8a"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28124": {"changesets": [{"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056732 - automatically download smart tab grouping models for Auto Tab Grouping  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315309\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320227\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AutoTabGroupingSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_group_tabs_button.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/SmartTabGrouping.sys.mjs", "testing/profiles/common/user.js"], "git_node": "bc27a4a1fda0675e22c17494fde0a92585d7f5bf", "git_parents": ["fa5662d6e39f8962e20c365e982759b914c65b8a"], "node": "2ffe99a90622698b885614a1da1024aa6d43d03c", "parents": ["1e495ce334000913a29fe27dbbcabe166040b61c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061856 - Let callers of removeAllDuplicateTabs anchor the confirmation hint  a=RyanVM\n\nremoveAllDuplicateTabs raises a confirmation hint (\"Closed N tabs\") anchored to\nthe All Tabs button. Now that the function can be called from elsewhere (ie the\nOrganize Tabs panel), the confirmation should point at the caller rather than\nstatically at the All Tabs button, which is removable and is not the button the\nuser pressed. With no All Tabs button on the toolbar there is nothing to anchor\nto and the hint lands in the corner of the window.\n\nTake the anchor as an option, defaulting to the All Tabs button so the All Tabs\nmenu is unchanged, and point the Smart Window \"Organize Tabs\" panel's Close\nDuplicate Tabs row at its own toolbar button.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317169\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320228\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AutoTabGrouping.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_group_tabs_button.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_multiselect_tabs_close_duplicate_tabs.js"], "git_node": "2870068e62d2c6e9ef73a1d0e4a06cfa24c9707a", "git_parents": ["bc27a4a1fda0675e22c17494fde0a92585d7f5bf"], "node": "5eb6b0338a1f3258870bc6f302bf79e5b041290e", "parents": ["2ffe99a90622698b885614a1da1024aa6d43d03c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787276747, "git_changesets": ["bc27a4a1fda0675e22c17494fde0a92585d7f5bf", "2870068e62d2c6e9ef73a1d0e4a06cfa24c9707a"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28125": {"changesets": [{"author": "Kaitlyn \u003ckandres@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062848 - Fix clipped digit visual issue on show trackers when resizing browser window.  a=RyanVM\n\nPlease see the recording in this ticket for the visual issue.\nhttps://mozilla-hub.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/FELTPY/boards/13722?selectedIssue=FELTPY-119\n\nAnother relevant Slack discussion: https://mozilla.slack.com/archives/C4D3JFF26/p1785182348472679\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318471\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320239\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/identity-block/identity-block.css"], "git_node": "cd9f782c31a081e6793b9012577dfa59724220f1", "git_parents": ["2870068e62d2c6e9ef73a1d0e4a06cfa24c9707a"], "node": "15a1d5036d56d93fda1e6559ad4a006df6e124a2", "parents": ["5eb6b0338a1f3258870bc6f302