03e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062950 - Move default browser prompt gating into DefaultBrowserPromptManager.  a=RyanVM\n\n**Fix**\n* Folded the Nimbus enabled check into `canShowPrompt()` alongside the existing device-capable, not-already-default, and not-yet-shown checks, instead of gating on it separately in `OnboardingFragment`.\n* Add tests covering the enabled-flag case and the `maybePromptToSetAsDefaultBrowser` integration path.\n\n**Expected behaviour**\nThe set to default system prompt should be shown during onboarding when:\n  - the device is capable\n  - the onboarding card is the set to default card\n  - Firefox (current build) is not already default browser\n  - the set to default prompt is enabled\n  - the prompt has not already been shown during onboarding\n\n{F77595754}\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318095\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320843\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/OverlayRegistry.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/DefaultBrowserPromptManager.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/OnboardingFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/DefaultBrowserPromptManagerTest.kt"], "git_node": "b64e2425042eac1207352ed8a24e81fa97e5251d", "git_parents": ["16d4eb63480ba6d35d8d6ca048a34b081766b981"], "node": "4de0db0387abc75ad5baba8df0a18f0e292cc193", "parents": ["8c22b5e076d6e0d192d842b538a0d7b1549ba698"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787590876, "git_changesets": ["b64e2425042eac1207352ed8a24e81fa97e5251d"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28195": {"changesets": [{"author": "Bryan Johns \u003cbjohns@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064790 - Set browser.smartwindow.searchTheWebFast default to true  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319871\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320881\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/search/SearchWorkflow.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "00efaea9cc256947b606ce09a215af4683d816a4", "git_parents": ["b64e2425042eac1207352ed8a24e81fa97e5251d"], "node": "081774e434893810b9d4e380e91a6b9a02700a70", "parents": ["4de0db0387abc75ad5baba8df0a18f0e292cc193"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787590898, "git_changesets": ["00efaea9cc256947b606ce09a215af4683d816a4"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28196": {"changesets": [{"author": "Harveer Singh \u003chsingh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054702: Perform principal validation in PQuotaRequests.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316654\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320965\n", "files": ["dom/quota/QuotaParent.cpp", "dom/quota/QuotaParent.h", "dom/tests/mochitest/localstorage/localStorageCommon.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/mochitest/test_ext_browsingData_indexedDB.html"], "git_node": "f3de5c56f553e3c17f428b25545dc5b1d0904c9f", "git_parents": ["00efaea9cc256947b606ce09a215af4683d816a4"], "node": "e4f242b9ddad7fa175a78f436b0f991b5af3d3cd", "parents": ["081774e434893810b9d4e380e91a6b9a02700a70"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787590930, "git_changesets": ["f3de5c56f553e3c17f428b25545dc5b1d0904c9f"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28197": {"changesets": [{"author": "Makoto Kato \u003cm_kato@ga2.so-net.ne.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061267 - Use std::string_view directly.  a=RyanVM\n\nCurrently, `FluentBuiltInNumberFormatterCreate` uses `std::string` to\npass the arguments as `std::string_view`. But this scope is incorrect.\n\nSimply, we should use `std::string_view` directly.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319982\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320799\n", "files": ["intl/l10n/FluentBundle.cpp"], "git_node": "155f7aedeabacf722169a4542709f42cb550a7d0", "git_parents": ["f3de5c56f553e3c17f428b25545dc5b1d0904c9f"], "node": "8dc377a1fc5af598de4a442e211ce03fd343e22f", "parents": ["e4f242b9ddad7fa175a78f436b0f991b5af3d3cd"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787590960, "git_changesets": ["155f7aedeabacf722169a4542709f42cb550a7d0"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28198": {"changesets": [{"author": "Stephen King \u003csking@thunderbird.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064906 - Add optional update_clobber_file to landoscript schemas.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nThis allows the clobber file to be optional for all lando-script merge\nautomation tasks.\n\nThis is particularly helpful for Thunderbird, which has no clobber file\nbut uses these merge automation actions\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319934\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320954\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/task.py"], "git_node": "9f6c1a5ab15aaa8d2175d0e59ae9acb41c0ad5d3", "git_parents": ["155f7aedeabacf722169a4542709f42cb550a7d0"], "node": "9f20949863c598844a05b90c3ad0e6c16a0e9e13", "parents": ["8dc377a1fc5af598de4a442e211ce03fd343e22f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787595802, "git_changesets": ["9f6c1a5ab15aaa8d2175d0e59ae9acb41c0ad5d3"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28199": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064321 - Emit repetitions for the surface's needs, not the tile cache dirty rect.  a=RyanVM\n\nprepare_repeatable_quad's \"repeat by duplicating the primitive\" path enumerated\nrepetitions against frame_state.current_dirty_region(), which is the picture\ncache tile's dirty region: push_dirty_region only happens for\nPictureCompositeMode::TileCache. Inside an intermediate surface that samples\noutside of its own footprint, the repetitions falling in that surface's\ninflation margin were dropped, so a blur read missing content and the wrong\nresult was baked into the picture cache tile with nothing left to invalidate it.\n\nCull against the current surface's clipping_rect instead. For a primitive drawn\nstraight onto a picture cache slice that is the dirty region (push_surface is\npassed surface_local_dirty_rect), so the optimisation is preserved; inside a\nfilter surface it is surface_rects.clipped_local, the inflated region that\nsurface needs. This is also the rect prepare_quad_impl already uses to decide\nwhat to draw, so the two now agree.\n\nprepare_image_quads' tiled path had the same bug, from the same\ncompute_conservative_visible_rect(current_dirty_region()) call. It is worse\nthere: that rect culls the repetitions and, within each repetition, the\nindividual texture cache tiles, so even a plain non-repeating tiled image loses\nthe tiles that fall in the blur's margin, and those tiles are never requested\nfrom the resource cache at all. Both callers now share\ncompute_surface_visible_rect, and compute_conservative_visible_rect goes away\nwith its last caller.\n\nThe reftests put a repeating gradient, a repeating tiled image and a plain tiled\nimage inside a horizontally blurred surface that straddles the x=1024 picture\ncache tile boundary, and invalidate only the tiles on one side of it so that the\ndirty region ends mid-surface. Each reference needs a first frame that\ninvalidates every tile: the harness renders the reference into the same wrench\ninstance right after the test, so a reference display list identical to the\ntest's last frame invalidates nothing and merely re-composites the test's own\ntiles, reproducing whatever the test got wrong.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319789\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320848\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/tiles/dirty-rect-blur-repeat-gradient-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/tiles/dirty-rect-blur-repeat-gradient.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/tiles/dirty-rect-blur-repeat-tiled-image-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/tiles/dirty-rect-blur-repeat-tiled-image.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/tiles/dirty-rect-blur-tiled-image-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/tiles/dirty-rect-blur-tiled-image.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/tiles/reftest.list"], "git_node": "9e687bf9bae43aa552a9c09b90a18de0f0fff9de", "git_parents": ["9f6c1a5ab15aaa8d2175d0e59ae9acb41c0ad5d3"], "node": "7c504b615add009107fd84be62de00c0c29cae10", "parents": ["9f20949863c598844a05b90c3ad0e6c16a0e9e13"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787595856, "git_changesets": ["9e687bf9bae43aa552a9c09b90a18de0f0fff9de"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28200": {"changesets": [{"author": "Sam Foster \u003csfoster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063204 - Hide the menu when clicking on the 'turn on sync' button.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319309\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320952\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-sync.js"], "git_node": "557de85c95c95271fa3ecdd75dc677587fbcfbf6", "git_parents": ["9e687bf9bae43aa552a9c09b90a18de0f0fff9de"], "node": "d571e6b6ab12fe58c3112b305ba58903b6fbca29", "parents": ["7c504b615add009107fd84be62de00c0c29cae10"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787595887, "git_changesets": ["557de85c95c95271fa3ecdd75dc677587fbcfbf6"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28201": {"changesets": [{"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065054 - Don't normalize image mask polygon points by the external scroll offset  a=RyanVM\n\npolygon_contains_point treats an ImageMaskClip's points as relative to the\nmask rect's origin, so they carry no external scroll offset. Shifting them\nin define_clip_image_mask displaced them from the already-normalized rect,\nculling every hit-test item under a clip-path: polygon() once its scroll\nframe had scrolled. Rendering was unaffected; only the hit tester reads the\npolygon.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320289\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321038\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_hittest_clippath_scrolled.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/test_group_hittest-2.html", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_list.rs"], "git_node": "0e1d9064001953a46127bd9217b41506e454d533", "git_parents": ["557de85c95c95271fa3ecdd75dc677587fbcfbf6"], "node": "eeab8c954805592c5eb47f6418110bd11764940e", "parents": ["d571e6b6ab12fe58c3112b305ba58903b6fbca29"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787602240, "git_changesets": ["0e1d9064001953a46127bd9217b41506e454d533"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28202": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 8b532c2140db30c193436254a61ce964e7d2a121 with FIREFOX_154_0_1_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "1b7abd8f650c807e5ce73430b6f8a0d97538ceaa", "git_parents": ["ae2897da461f971bead79663a03cbf771f85b6c0"], "node": "a583d46f590901ff651cd01ac15a6e49816f1d83", "parents": ["6e5e2296e2e27ad31714a1ed92d540de930776ca"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787602663, "git_changesets": ["1b7abd8f650c807e5ce73430b6f8a0d97538ceaa"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "28203": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 8b532c2140db30c193436254a61ce964e7d2a121 with FIREFOX-ANDROID_154_0_1_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "4fce20f036b0cf1fe3fad9ff62d5b7180727e14c", "git_parents": ["1b7abd8f650c807e5ce73430b6f8a0d97538ceaa"], "node": "9c20d772368fae616c220c8c4309ca58924592dd", "parents": ["a583d46f590901ff651cd01ac15a6e49816f1d83"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787602732, "git_c